---
code: cli-strip-got-a-flag
when-fires: dorc strip got a positional that starts with a dash. cli/lib.rs parse_args_from. {got} is the token found.
why: AID-NEEDS:law-codes-vary-by-world-not-grammar: the SIBLING of cli-strip-needs-path - an argument WAS given, so the user asked for a surface strip does not have, and the remediation differs.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc strip --book=webhost.sh
dorc: error[cli-strip-got-a-flag]: `dorc strip` takes only a file path, but was
given the flag `--book=webhost.sh`.
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [-o <oracle.sh>]... [--debug-argv]
